Third-party content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section records what in this repository was not written here, and on what
terms it is present. It was compiled by audit rather than by memory; the audit
and its method are written up in docs/reports/m15.md.

1. NO VENDORED SOURCE CODE.

   aipcb vendors no third-party code. In particular the S-expression reader and
   writer in src/aipcb/kicad/sexpr.py is original work, written for this project
   after `kiutils` was evaluated and rejected; the reasoning is recorded in
   docs/decisions/0001-kicad-io.md. It is not derived from `kiutils` or from
   KiCad's own parser.

2. KiCad SYMBOL AND FOOTPRINT DATA, embedded in generated design files.

   The example designs reference stock KiCad library symbols and footprints by
   name (for instance `Connector:Bus_PCI_Express_x1`). KiCad, in the ordinary
   course of writing a schematic, inlines the referenced symbol definitions into
   the `.kicad_sch` file, and footprint geometry into the `.kicad_pcb` file. The
   generated designs committed under examples/ and tests/golden/ therefore
   contain KiCad library data.

   The KiCad libraries are licensed CC-BY-SA 4.0 with an exception:

       To the extent that the creation of electronic designs that use
       'Licensed Material' can be considered to be 'Adapted Material', then
       the copyright holder waives article 3 of the license with respect to
       these designs and any generated files which use data provided as part
       of the 'Licensed Material'.

   The files here are exactly that: generated files which use library data. The
   exception applies, and the share-alike article does not reach them. The
   exception is withdrawn only for redistributing the libraries "as a collection";
   this repository contains no `.kicad_sym`, no `.kicad_mod`, no `.pretty`
   directory and no library table — the audit checked. Attribution is offered
   here as courtesy rather than obligation:

       KiCad Libraries — https://gitlab.com/kicad/libraries
       Copyright the KiCad Librarian Team and contributors
       CC-BY-SA 4.0 with the design exception above
       https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/

3. EXTERNAL TOOLS, INVOKED AND NEVER EMBEDDED.

   aipcb runs several third-party programs as separate processes and exchanges
   files with them. It does not link against them, import them, bundle them, or
   distribute them, and none of their licences reach aipcb's own code:

       KiCad 9.x           GPL-3.0-or-later   invoked as `kicad-cli`, and as a
                                              `pcbnew` subprocess that imports
                                              nothing from aipcb (ADR 0009)
       Freerouting 2.x     GPL-3.0            invoked by the user or agent; aipcb
                                              only writes DSN and reads SES
       openEMS             GPL-3.0            run inside a container image
       gerber2ems          Apache-2.0         run inside the same container image

   The `pcbnew` boundary is deliberate and is documented in
   docs/decisions/0009-pours.md: aipcb's own process never imports `pcbnew`, and
   the helper subprocess that does imports nothing from aipcb and nothing outside
   the standard library. The container image for openEMS and gerber2ems is built
   by the user from Antmicro's published Dockerfile; it is not distributed here.

4. RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES.

   Every distribution in aipcb's runtime dependency closure is BSD/MIT-family or
   equivalently permissive — 16 distributions, measured, at the time of writing.
   tools/check_licenses.py re-measures this and fails CI on drift, so the claim
   has an expiry date attached to it rather than a date of writing.

5. TECHNICAL STANDARDS AND DATASHEETS.

   Connector pinouts in examples/library/ (PCI Express card edge, SATA, USB
   Micro-B) are factual contact assignments, not copied expression. Where a
   specification's requirements are discussed — the SATA skew tables in
   examples/pcie-sata/design.yaml, for example — they are cited and paraphrased,
   never reproduced. No datasheet text is included verbatim. One datasheet URL is
   linked, not mirrored.
